WEBVTT

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:08.420
Stepping out on
an ordinary Sunday

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:14.930
Stepping out!
A miracle's gonna happen

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.760
It's my day!

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:27.340
Maybe I'll throw off my pajamas

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:34.750
and head out to see her right now

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:42.120
I always turned my eyes away,
thinking she'd hate me

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:49.530
Now I'm saying goodbye
to that negative attitude

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:55.300
My favorite shoes
will always take me

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:02.440
To a place where I'll be happy

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:09.950
It's not someone else
I want to embrace

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:16.090
But a version of
myself that's not fake

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:19.160
I just want to walk

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:22.690
Not on tip-toe

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:26.660
Not downcast, either

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:35.570
Just I'm stepping out
on an ordinary Sunday

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:42.010
Stepping out!
Making a little try, try, try

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:44.280
It's my day!

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:04.430
<i>Shizuka's moving to France.</i>

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.700
<i>Shizuka's special to Rui Hanazawa.</i>

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:11.240
<i>But...</i>

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.680
<i>...Rui Hanazawa's special to me.</i>

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.130
Will I ever be special to Rui Hanazawa?

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:42.240
"Love Beyond The Horizon"

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:47.710
Hey!

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:55.410
What is it?

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:58.280
Don't you have something
to say to me?

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:59.190
Hm? Um...

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:00.650
Idiot.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:01.650
No!

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:05.790
Bonehead?

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:11.630
You! Don't tell me you forgot!

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:14.040
You blew chunks on
my Ermani suit!

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:20.710
That was bad... I really don't
remember much.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:23.010
Hey, girls! Here's our big chance!

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:27.650
With Shizuka in Paris,
Hanazawa will be fair game, right?

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.780
If we can sneak our way
into his heart...

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:38.960
<i>I...</i>

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:42.260
You're just like them!

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:45.740
You're so happy about it, you can't
think of anything else!

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.940
And Rui... what's 
going to happen to him?

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:05.980
<i>I...!</i>

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:10.420
Hey!

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.970
<i>What was I thinking?!</i>

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.460
<i>I'm acting just like 
the people I hate most!</i>

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:23.100
<i>I'm such a coward... such a coward...</i>

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:24.630
<i>This is not me...</i>

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.520
<i>...thinking only about myself,
and not the one I care about!</i>

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:37.860
<i>I should want what's best for him...</i>

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:44.630
Shizuka!

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:50.730
Makino! What's the hurry?

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:53.450
I'm sorry about the other night!

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:56.630
I wanted you to come,
but things got weird...

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.240
I've just told the school
I'll be leaving.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.480
Shizuka! Please don't go to France!

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:07.540
Huh?

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:11.280
You could study to become
a lawyer here, couldn't you?

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.420
Makino, calm down!
What's the matter?

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:24.160
Please!

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.270
I know it's none of my business, but...

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:32.570
You've got to stay in Japan!

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.070
For Rui Hanazawa's sake!

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:36.600
You've got to stay!

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:55.260
<i>I'd always look forward to seeing
Rui Hanazawa on the stairs.</i>

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:01.450
<i>The feeling of disappointment when
he wasn't there...</i>

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:03.000
<i>I know better than anyone.</i>

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:08.730
<i>And even worse, the thought of never 
seeing the one you love again...</i>

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:12.470
Makino...

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:17.310
I can't stay.

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:20.090
I just can't.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.470
I know you can't.

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:34.160
I know I'm asking the impossible...

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:35.910
Makino...

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:39.430
<i>...but this is the only thing
I can do!</i>

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.030
Please, Shizuka!

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:49.510
<i>I am who I am.</i>

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:54.360
Makino, look at me.

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.270
Listen, Makino.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:02.530
When I see an opportunity,
I have to take it.

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:05.390
It's like shopping
in a foreign country.

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:11.140
If I get on an airplane
without buying something...

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:13.880
I may never be able
to purchase it.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:20.970
Some spend their lives thinking of
what they <i>should</i> have done.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:24.340
I don't want to end up that way.
That's why I'm going.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:28.880
Shizuka...

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:37.720
Please forgive me.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:40.910
No need! You make me happy.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:44.530
You've really had an impact here.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:47.960
Not everyone could deal
with Tsukasa's bunch.

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:50.170
Oh, no...

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:03.700
Goodbye. I really do like you.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:05.650
Shizuka...

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:18.090
I like you, too.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:25.870
<i>I idolized you so much. 
You had everything a girl could want.</i>

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:33.220
<i>But you've given it all up
to follow your dreams.</i>

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:40.210
<i>I'm glad Rui Hanazawa
is in love with you.</i>

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:54.390
<i>Rui Hanazawa!</i>

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.200
What was that all about?!

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:00.000
Who asked you to say anything?

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:03.140
"For my sake"?!
How can you say that?

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:06.510
Who asked <i>you</i> to butt in?

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:17.100
What were you thinking?
Pleading with her that way...

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:26.890
How could you do that?

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:30.060
It's unbelievable!

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.010
W-well...

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:46.000
You were so sad sad.
You might never see her again...

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.380
That's none of your business!

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:56.350
Go away!

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:58.620
Go!

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:16.370
Damn it!

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:24.140
<i>Maybe it is none of my business...</i>

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:26.150
<i>But...</i>

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:36.830
<i>This is... the elementary school.</i>

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:55.980
<i>I don't even know half of what
they know about each other.</i>

00:10:56.810 --> 00:10:57.670
<i>But still...</i>

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:08.720
Ms. Urara?

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:12.900
Memories are strange things.

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:19.060
Someday, you might treasure even
the most painful memories.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:38.420
Someday, I might treasure even
the most painful memories...

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:07.710
Hey, did you reach Rui?

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:11.410
No. I've been calling since yesterday,
but he hasn't answered.

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:14.820
Shizuka's leaving!
What the hell's he doing?

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:27.400
<i>Why isn't he here?</i>

00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:34.570
<i>He may never see her again.</i>

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:39.580
I'll try him one more time.

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:41.070
I'll come with you.

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:44.940
What's in the box?

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:47.710
A going-away present for Shizuka.
Wanna see?

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:49.590
Sure!

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:56.660
Got ya!

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:03.160
<i>If only Rui Hanazawa could have 
a fragment of his easygoing nature...</i>

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.470
What's with the long face?

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.410
You look even uglier than usual.

00:13:09.710 --> 00:13:10.740
Domyoji...

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:13.010
Have you ever loved someone?

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:14.170
What?

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:18.180
<i>She hasn't got a clue.</i>

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:22.920
Is that what love is like?

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:25.590
<i>Who asked you to butt in?</i>

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:31.100
Is it really healthy to repress
your feelings?

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:34.430
Is it okay to let things end
that way?

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:37.070
No, that'd be stupid.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:39.830
It's like there wasn't a relationship
to begin with.

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:42.930
<i>How simple...</i>

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:45.640
That's just common sense.

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:47.610
<i>...and yet, so profound.</i>

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:49.410
What if you died tomorrow?

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:51.340
You will regret it forever.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:55.780
You... you... might actually be smart!

00:13:57.290 --> 00:13:59.150
You mean you just realized?

00:14:00.260 --> 00:14:02.640
<i>Neither Rui Hanazawa nor I
could figure that out...</i>

00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:04.620
<i>...but Tsukasa did without
a moment's thought.</i>

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:09.900
No good...

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:11.170
...no answer.

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:12.570
Man, Rui's such a jerk!

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:26.950
<i>Rui Hanazawa...</i>

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:33.120
We'll miss you!

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:38.960
<i>Are you really not coming?</i>

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:45.980
<i>Departing passengers
on flight 284 for Paris...</i>

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:50.000
<i>...please proceed to the gate
for boarding.</i>

00:14:50.310 --> 00:14:51.240
It's time.

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:57.250
<i>Shizuka...</i>

00:14:58.310 --> 00:14:59.380
Take care, Shizuka.

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:00.280
Thanks...

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:02.720
Keep in touch, okay?

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:03.380
Sure!

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:05.750
Shizuka, I got this for you...

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:08.290
Thanks, Tsukasa!

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:10.890
Good luck, Shizuka.

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:12.360
Take care of yourself...

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:13.060
You too.

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:14.630
I'll miss you, everybody!

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:18.900
<i>Is this how you want it to end,
Rui Hanazawa?</i>

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:27.410
Please give Rui my regards.

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:28.580
Sure.

00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:37.850
Bye!

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:39.190
Good luck!

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:41.250
Don't forget to write!

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:42.390
Stay well!

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:43.960
Come back soon!

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:54.800
<i>And then she left, to the sound of
her many friends' happy farewells.</i>

00:15:56.400 --> 00:16:00.140
<i>I'm not sure I'll meet
such a wonderful person ever again.</i>

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:21.430
<i>I can picture her walking around Paris, 
trading in her fabulous dresses for jeans...</i>

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:24.640
<i>When you wear beautiful shoes...</i>

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:27.370
<i>...they will take you
to beautiful places.</i>

00:16:40.010 --> 00:16:42.170
Well, she's in the sky now...

00:16:42.170 --> 00:16:44.130
What do we do? 
Mess around and head home?

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:46.950
Rui never showed up.
What a jerk.

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:05.900
<i>R-Rui Hanazawa?!</i>

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:07.070
Rui!

00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:10.740
Where were you?! Shizuka's gone.

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:12.480
How long have you been here?

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:13.980
About an hour.

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:18.220
Did you see Shizuka?

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:20.720
From behind a pillar.

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:22.250
Behind a pillar?!

00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:29.760
You go after her!

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:35.500
If you love her, go after her!

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:38.270
Was watching from behind a pillar
enough for you?

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:40.270
What kind of a man are you?!

00:17:40.970 --> 00:17:43.370
I know you're the kind who
hangs out with these three...

00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:45.640
...that's why you don't get it!

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:04.200
I've got a seat
on the next flight.

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:07.400
Seriously, Rui?

00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:09.460
Way to go!!

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:17.000
Makino...
I really love that part of you.

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:19.340
You have a strength I don't.

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:23.480
It made me realize... that I couldn't
let it end like this.

00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:26.480
Thank you.

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:43.710
Good luck!

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:44.970
Call us when you get there!

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:47.930
<i>I was speechless.</i>

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:55.440
<i>His eyes, like marbles...
his soft brown hair...</i>

00:18:56.310 --> 00:19:00.080
<i>...his moss green sweater...
all blurred together in my tears.</i>

00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:18.500
Rui finally came through!

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:21.670
But it was Makino who convinced him.

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:25.200
Didn't she have a crush on him?

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:31.440
It's like I've been saying all along...
no chance!

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:34.550
Right!

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:36.150
He never said that, did he?

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:37.350
Whatever.

00:19:38.850 --> 00:19:41.950
I'll miss the guy, though.

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:44.520
He'll be back some day.

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:54.800
Bye-bye, Rui Hanazawa.

00:20:49.650 --> 00:20:50.590
Makino...

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:55.720
...let's go on a date.

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:02.630
What was that?

00:21:02.930 --> 00:21:05.610
Got it? I'll tell you the day later.

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:07.480
<i>What was he saying?</i>

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:09.570
Let's go.

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:12.120
Wait, Domyoji!

00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:21.450
<i>What's with him?
What was he saying?</i>

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:24.950
Tsukushi... Let's go home.

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:25.650
Okay.

00:21:45.270 --> 00:21:47.440
<i>Oh, well... whatever.</i>

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:11.600
You let your hair down a little

00:22:13.570 --> 00:22:19.470
You hid the fact
that you were crying

00:22:21.240 --> 00:22:29.350
I noticed, but I
couldn't ask you why

00:22:29.580 --> 00:22:37.390
I can never be
honest about how I feel

00:22:37.390 --> 00:22:45.160
Until after we've split
up after a bad fight

00:22:45.430 --> 00:22:53.300
I can say it now,
though, over and over

00:22:45.430 --> 00:22:53.300
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:22:53.300 --> 00:23:01.680
I can say "I love you"...

00:22:53.300 --> 00:23:01.680
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:11.460
Do you really hate me this time?

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:19.230
Will you end up running to him?

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:27.400
I can say it now,
though, over and over

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:27.400
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:35.810
I can say "I love you"...

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:35.810
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:50.090
Rui Hanazawa flew to Paris
to follow Shizuka.

00:23:50.630 --> 00:23:52.460
I wonder what he's doing now...

00:23:53.330 --> 00:23:57.200
But while I was wondering,
Tsukasa came up to me...

00:23:57.270 --> 00:23:59.030
...said something, and left.

00:23:59.640 --> 00:24:01.870
I wonder what he's thinking...

00:24:03.140 --> 00:24:06.610
Next on Hana Yori Dango:
"A Date in the Snow"

00:24:07.240 --> 00:24:09.410
You can pay me back,
if you like.
